   "id": "01-problem",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Problem\n",
    "\n",
    "A lender commits money before knowing whether it comes back. We predict the **probability of default** using only what is known at application time.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two errors, unequal costs: **approving a defaulter** loses most of the principal; **rejecting a good borrower** loses only the profit on that loan. We assume the first mistake costs **5×** more — that asymmetry drives every downstream decision on threshold and pricing.\n",
    "\n",
    "Live app: **http://eab-credit.preview.james-benjamin.com/**"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
